  "body": "Capture/refund arithmetic previously added Int64 values before checking the ceiling, admitting wrapped negative results. This change checks remaining capacity first and accumulates ledger entries as Integer. It also repairs exact PlusCal regeneration, makes formal CI retain fresh source/tool receipts, and reuses the canonical identity-preserving release recovery guard from #453.\n\nThe actual Haskell arithmetic oracle now runs in the standard Hspec suite (`stack test`), addressing the review on the standalone probe: 400 transition cases and 512 ledger cases, with input-specific failures. The compatibility probe delegates to that suite; CI no longer relies on a bespoke invocation.\n\nCanonical scope, authority, requirement traceability, conflicts, assumptions and reproduction commands are in [formal/system/README.md](formal/system/README.md) and [the delivery report](formal/system/delivery-2026-09-20.md). Existing domain specifications remain authoritative within their stated approval and rollout boundaries. The discovery inventory covers 492 artifacts, 243 requirements/candidates and 119 model configurations; the separate pinned mobile tree is also inventoried. Complete semantic rule extraction and global cross-domain refinement remain open.\n\nValidation at implementation `633f9f906e7cb9d9a0911887fc057ca7ff68906c`: source-derived Z3 safety/admission obligations UNSAT over the full signed Int64 domain with documented preconditions; positive witnesses and legacy counterexamples SAT; three verifier regressions passed; 912 actual-Haskell oracle cases passed; complete local repository gate passed. Local and [hosted formal execution](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/actions/runs/35551938342) have the same source digest. [Social model/persistence checks](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/actions/runs/35551938226) passed. These are qualified arithmetic/model/test results, not whole-system implementation verification; the remaining combined CI run was superseded by the final integration.\n\nCurrent head `6fbae058e23c989599116c629a80fe216505c1e4` integrates protected main `3d0b43942e3db9597cd159ffa37bf10713069a0b`, including #451's records availability migration. Fresh [CI](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/actions/runs/35553494963), [formal](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/actions/runs/35553495038) and [social](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/actions/runs/35553494806) checks apply to this integration. The final release now requires a matching 114-entry recovery manifest; the old 113-entry image is ineligible. This PR introduces no new migration beyond concurrent main.\n\nNo production deployment, mobile publication, provider activation or real financial transaction has been performed by this audit. Independent current-head approval, protected merge, exact-image staging and guarded production rollout remain required. PaymentIntentStore uses the repaired function, but no current HTTP/worker caller of that adapter was found; no live corruption/outage is claimed.\n\n\nSYS-D06 fixes a confirmed inventory omission: backend-local specs, OpenAPI fragments, component READMEs and technical root guidance now appear in canonical discovery. Three regression checks enforce coverage, private/evidence exclusions and preservation of inferred authority. Legacy escrow's nominal Payment-row rule is recorded as superseded by accepted ADR 0101. Seven corrective requirements are now traced; complete semantic extraction remains open.\n\nThe standard hosted Hspec run on `633f9f906` included the new oracle and reported 3,510 examples with zero failures and six pending database-script entrypoints; the integration lane invokes those separate scripts. This does not turn pending examples into proof. The arithmetic-oracle review thread is resolved; fresh independent approval is still required for the current head.\n",
